# Styling and DOM hooks

## Tailwind CSS v4 first

- Prefer **Tailwind v4 utility classes** in markup (`class="..."`) over ad‑hoc custom CSS classes.
- Add **custom CSS** only when utilities cannot express the design (complex selectors, one-off animations, third-party overrides). Keep bespoke class names minimal and purposeful.

## JavaScript hooks

- Use dedicated classes prefixed with **`js-`** for DOM queries and behavior (e.g. `js-archive-filters`, `js-year-range`). Do not rely on styling or Tailwind classes as JS selectors.

## Theme variables

- Reuse tokens from **`src/css/theme.css`**: `:root` (`--c-*`, layout tokens) and `@theme` (`--color-*`, `--font-*`, shadows, etc.).
- In Tailwind arbitrary values, prefer theme-backed CSS variables, e.g. `text-(--color-body)`, `bg-(--color-page)`.

## New tokens

- **Do not invent new theme variables** without confirmation. If no suitable token exists, **ask** whether to extend `theme.css` (and how to name/group the token) before adding one.
